    "reviewName": "blink-hooded_oriole",
    "title": "hooded oriole \u2014 blink repair appearance",
    "summary": "New blink source HELD in raw and codec,0/1 useful blink clips. The unchanged neutral/look remain readable reused source art; the new family is not complete at this normal-size blink bar.",
    "clips": [
      {
        "id": "new blink",
        "verdict": "HELD_RAW_AND_CODEC_0_OF_1",
        "reason": "The changed lid/eye-area detail remains too subtle against the black facial mask to identify unambiguously as closure during100ms at normal141CSS. It is a real source change, but a native close-up and color differences cannot establish normal-size semantic recognition."
      },
      {
        "id": "existing look and neutral",
        "verdict": "PROVISIONALLY_USEFUL_REUSE",
        "reason": "Retained identity and readable attention/neutral posture. No new look or neutral drawing/gain is claimed."
      }
    ],
    "normalSizeFinding": "Actual141CSS/density1 raw and codec, light/dark. Broad identity, body scale and feet remain coherent without conspicuous body jump, deep crouch or long-leg reach. Mild contour/toe detail shimmer is secondary, not the held reason. Own live blink60/3/27@30Hz observes60/61/62closedphase, exactneutral63 return and89heldthrough3000ms. Existing look60/6/24 also returns to the same neutral. No page errors; images inspected only in memory.",
    "qualifications": "The normal-size recognition criterion remains unchanged; neither genuine native closure, technical/palette success nor matching bounds substitutes for readable closure. No inference of physical pressure/support. Runtime NOT_SUBMITTED/NOT_TESTED for the failed new blink; no automatic retry or reviewer generation. Source originals/all attempts and prior held results remain unchanged.",
    "usefulNewBlinkClips": 0,
    "possibleNewBlinkClips": 1,
    "handoffFile": "family-handoff.json"
  },
